+class GridPatchDataset(IterableDataset):
+    """
+    Yields patches from image items in a dataset. A patch generator, such as :py:class:`PatchIter`, samples each image
+    on a contiguous grid, and an optional transform is applied to each patch. Each element is the patch, or a
+    (patch, coordinates) pair when `with_coordinates` is True. The coordinates are an integer array with one
+    ``[start, stop]`` row per dimension of the image, channel included.
+
+    For example, two single-channel 4x4 images sampled with 2x2 patches give eight patches of shape (1, 2, 2). Each
+    coordinate array has shape (3, 2), and the first patch of the first image has coordinates
+    ``[[0, 1], [0, 2], [0, 2]]``:
